WEBVTT

02:16.942 --> 02:21.703
What'd you think, you
paired up with him?

02:21.736 --> 02:25.667
What'd I think?

02:25.708 --> 02:27.802
Well, you don't pick
your parents,

02:27.843 --> 02:31.270
and you don't pick your partner.

02:31.303 --> 02:36.939
You know, they used to call
him The Tax Man for a while?

02:36.972 --> 02:40.573
He'd come out of Texas,
so nobody knew him.

02:40.606 --> 02:42.907
Seemed a bit...

02:42.940 --> 02:46.504
raw-boned to me, edgy.

02:46.537 --> 02:47.976
Took 3 months till we got him

02:48.009 --> 02:50.880
over to the house for dinner.

02:50.913 --> 02:52.711
Around our big 419.

02:52.744 --> 02:55.183
That's what y'all want
to hear about, right,

02:55.216 --> 02:57.984
Dora Lange, kids in the woods?

02:58.017 --> 03:01.715
Yeah, sure,
but, uh, talk about Cohle.

03:01.748 --> 03:03.386
We heard some stories.

03:03.419 --> 03:06.820
Kind of a strange guy, huh?

03:06.853 --> 03:10.720
Strange. Uh... heh, heh, heh.

03:10.753 --> 03:12.561
Yeah.

03:12.894 --> 03:16.092
Rust would pick a fight
with the sky

03:16.125 --> 03:20.896
if he didn't like
its shade of blue,

03:20.929 --> 03:23.833
but when we finally got
him over to the house...

03:23.866 --> 03:25.967
this is when that case
was hot...

03:26.000 --> 03:28.164
poor bastard looked like
he was on his way

03:28.197 --> 03:31.702
to the firing squad.

03:31.735 --> 03:34.237
Dora Lange.

03:34.270 --> 03:37.844
Yeah. Occult ritual murder.

03:37.877 --> 03:41.210
You can thank
the "Advertiser" for that.

03:41.243 --> 03:42.523
Could you, uh, hold off on that?

03:42.548 --> 03:44.716
All right. Yeah. You can't
do that here no more.

03:44.749 --> 03:47.749
- Huh?
- Uh-uh.

03:47.790 --> 03:49.188
Don't be assholes.

03:49.221 --> 03:51.293
You want to hear this or not?

04:08.666 --> 04:12.265
Vermillion sheriff requested
assistance with a 419,

04:12.298 --> 04:16.369
cane fields outside of Erath.

04:16.402 --> 04:18.370
I'd been on the job
about 3 months till then.

04:18.410 --> 04:24.176
Two previous cases
were open and shut.

04:24.209 --> 04:29.758
It was January 3, 1995,
my daughter's birthday.

04:29.791 --> 04:31.055
I remember.

04:55.859 --> 04:59.731
Hart and Cohle, State CID.

04:59.764 --> 05:01.772
Who found her?

05:01.805 --> 05:02.932
Farmer and his son.

05:02.973 --> 05:04.971
This spread wasn't
scheduled for a burn.

05:05.004 --> 05:08.336
Let's keep them here, and
let's tape off this road,

05:08.369 --> 05:12.345
and give me your log.

05:15.810 --> 05:16.810
You take the log.

05:16.816 --> 05:18.013
Yes, sir.

05:18.046 --> 05:20.379
Make sure you get
everything down.

05:34.031 --> 05:35.597
Go ahead.

05:58.997 --> 06:00.763
You ever see
something like this?

06:00.796 --> 06:05.269
No, sir, in 8 years of CID.

06:05.302 --> 06:08.899
Them symbols, they's Satanic.

06:08.940 --> 06:12.570
They had a "20/20"
on it a few years back.

06:12.603 --> 06:14.006
ID?

06:14.039 --> 06:16.872
No, sir.

06:16.905 --> 06:21.179
We're gonna need
more men for a grid search,

06:21.212 --> 06:25.020
set up a perimeter wide as
possible on those 3 roads,

06:25.053 --> 06:26.924
post up, take license plates

06:26.957 --> 06:29.892
of anything that passes.

06:29.925 --> 06:31.027
I-23.

06:31.060 --> 06:33.459
Go ahead, I-23.

06:33.492 --> 06:37.625
We're gonna need investigator
assist on that 419,

06:37.667 --> 06:39.868
all you can spare for a canvass.

06:39.901 --> 06:41.268
Roger that, Detective.

06:41.301 --> 06:43.974
CID is taking over. Get
anybody who's free up here.

06:44.007 --> 06:47.047
Okay. Tell me
what you see.

06:47.080 --> 06:51.320
Ligature marks on her
wrists, ankles, and knees.

06:51.353 --> 06:54.615
Multiple shallow
stab wounds to the abdomen.

06:54.655 --> 06:56.750
Hemorrhaging around throat,

06:56.791 --> 07:01.361
lividity at the shoulders,
thighs, and torso.

07:01.394 --> 07:05.264
She'd been on her back a while

07:05.297 --> 07:07.566
before he moved her.

07:14.672 --> 07:17.608
That's why
they called him The Tax Man.

07:17.641 --> 07:20.848
The rest of us had these
little note pads or something.

07:20.881 --> 07:23.512
He had this big ledger.

07:23.552 --> 07:28.456
Looked funny walking door to
door with it like the tax man,

07:28.489 --> 07:33.126
which ain't bad
as far as nicknames go.

07:33.159 --> 07:36.660
Yeah. Of course
I've always taken a lot of notes.

07:36.693 --> 07:40.430
I mean, you never know what
the thing's gonna be, do you?

07:40.463 --> 07:43.197
A little detail
somewhere way down the line

07:43.230 --> 07:48.601
makes you say, "Ohh!"
breaks the case.

07:48.634 --> 07:50.970
You know, I've seen
all the different types.

07:51.003 --> 07:54.411
We all fit a certain category...

07:54.444 --> 08:01.918
the bully, the charmer,
the, uh, surrogate dad,

08:01.951 --> 08:06.393
the man possessed
by ungovernable rage,

08:06.426 --> 08:07.930
the brain...

08:07.963 --> 08:13.736
and any of those types
could be a good detective,

08:13.769 --> 08:18.472
and any of those types could be
an incompetent shitheel.

08:18.505 --> 08:20.743
Which type were you?

08:20.776 --> 08:26.216
Oh, I was just
a regular type dude

08:26.249 --> 08:28.951
with a big-ass dick.

08:31.048 --> 08:34.118
A lot of it had to do
with how they manage authority.

08:36.454 --> 08:42.325
There can be a burden
in authority, in vigilance,

08:42.358 --> 08:46.333
like a father's burden.

08:46.366 --> 08:48.902
It was too much for some men.

08:48.935 --> 08:53.303
A smart guy who's steady
is hard to find.

08:53.343 --> 08:55.774
I was all right,
better than some,

08:55.807 --> 09:02.846
but, you know, I knew how to talk
to people, and I was steady.

09:02.879 --> 09:07.456
Rust... now his
Texas files were classified

09:07.489 --> 09:12.059
or redacted,
and he wasn't big on talking

09:12.100 --> 09:15.669
except when you wanted
him to shut up,

09:15.702 --> 09:18.342
but he was smart.

09:22.246 --> 09:25.713
Yeah. Second week
we were together,

09:25.746 --> 09:28.448
I saw where he was living.

09:28.482 --> 09:30.816
Kind of made me feel
for the guy.

09:43.834 --> 09:45.137
I'd offer you a seat,

09:45.170 --> 09:47.842
but, uh...

09:47.875 --> 09:51.746
Don't mention it.
I, uh... I can't stay.

09:55.715 --> 09:56.849
Yeah, I'll tell you guys...

09:56.882 --> 09:59.452
and believe me,
past a certain age,

09:59.485 --> 10:04.155
a man without a family
can be a bad thing.

10:32.454 --> 10:37.794
We'd
encountered a meta-psychotic,

10:37.835 --> 10:40.495
which I had to explain to Marty,

10:40.528 --> 10:43.968
what meta-psychotic was.

10:47.732 --> 10:50.235
This is gonna happen again,

10:50.268 --> 10:56.244
or it's happened before, both.

10:56.309 --> 10:59.347
Go on.

10:59.380 --> 11:03.349
It's fantasy enactment, ritual,

11:03.382 --> 11:06.689
fetishization, iconography.

11:06.730 --> 11:08.498
This is his vision.

11:08.532 --> 11:12.402
Her body is
a paraphilic love map.

11:12.435 --> 11:14.069
How's that?

11:14.102 --> 11:16.311
An attachment of physical lust

11:16.344 --> 11:20.014
to fantasies and practices
forbidden by society.

11:22.384 --> 11:24.987
You get that from one
of your books?

11:25.020 --> 11:28.628
I did.

11:28.661 --> 11:32.365
Her knees are abraded,
rug burns on her back.

11:32.398 --> 11:34.163
Cold sores, gum line recession,

11:34.196 --> 11:35.395
bad teeth.

11:35.435 --> 11:38.498
There's decent odds
she was a prost.

11:38.531 --> 11:41.801
He might not have
known her, but...

11:41.834 --> 11:47.906
this idea goes
way back with him.

11:47.947 --> 11:50.440
You... you got a chapter
in one of those books

11:50.481 --> 11:53.846
on jumping to conclusions?

11:53.879 --> 11:56.551
You attach an assumption
to a piece of evidence,

11:56.584 --> 12:01.180
you start to bend the
narrative to support it,

12:01.221 --> 12:03.517
prejudice yourself.

12:06.590 --> 12:08.891
Wait and see on the ID.

12:12.429 --> 12:14.058
All right.

12:14.099 --> 12:18.801
This kind of thing does
not happen in a vacuum.

12:18.834 --> 12:22.538
I guarantee this
wasn't his first.

12:22.571 --> 12:24.201
It's too specific.

12:32.012 --> 12:33.451
Uh...

12:37.353 --> 12:40.456
listen, uh... ahem,
this is

12:40.489 --> 12:42.658
a...

12:42.690 --> 12:46.224
stupid time to mention this,

12:46.257 --> 12:48.561
but...

12:48.594 --> 12:51.999
you've got to come to dinner.

12:52.032 --> 12:53.663
Can't put Maggie off anymore,

12:53.697 --> 12:56.633
so you just got to.

13:03.377 --> 13:04.882
All right.

13:12.051 --> 13:14.089
Gordon, thanks for coming.

13:14.122 --> 13:15.592
Marty.

13:15.625 --> 13:17.655
Yeah. So...

13:17.688 --> 13:19.993
Anyway, that
evening, wasn't even sundown,

13:20.026 --> 13:23.559
he decided it was a good time
to invite me over for dinner,

13:23.600 --> 13:25.526
which I got a problem with,

13:25.566 --> 13:27.231
all right, because I'm
thinking about Marty's wife

13:27.264 --> 13:31.968
and this two kids and how
it's my daughter's birthday,

13:32.009 --> 13:33.472
and I know...

13:36.176 --> 13:37.974
there's nothing I can
do about it,

13:38.007 --> 13:42.512
maybe not today,
maybe not tomorrow, but...

13:42.553 --> 13:45.217
I'm gonna have a drink.

13:46.458 --> 13:47.457
Let me get up!
Heh, heh!

13:47.490 --> 13:48.951
Daddy!

13:48.992 --> 13:51.223
You're gonna meet him.
I got to get the door.

13:55.193 --> 13:57.127
Hey.

13:57.160 --> 14:00.502
Santa Claus is coming!

14:00.535 --> 14:04.035
Aah! Jump!
Ha, ha, ha!

14:12.972 --> 14:14.778
People out here,

14:14.811 --> 14:20.781
it's like they don't even know
the outside world exists.

14:20.822 --> 14:23.652
Might as well be living
on the fucking Moon.

14:25.786 --> 14:29.026
There's all kinds
of ghettos in the world.

14:29.059 --> 14:32.594
It's all one ghetto, man,

14:32.627 --> 14:35.560
giant gutter in outer space.

14:39.605 --> 14:43.508
Today, that scene,

14:43.541 --> 14:47.282
that is the most fucked
up thing I ever caught.

14:49.387 --> 14:51.648
Ask you something?

14:51.689 --> 14:55.490
You're a Christian, yeah?

14:55.523 --> 14:58.059
No.

14:58.100 --> 15:02.560
Well, then what do you got the
cross for in your apartment?

15:02.601 --> 15:06.765
That's a form of meditation.

15:06.798 --> 15:08.166
How's that?

15:11.169 --> 15:14.970
I contemplate
the moment in the garden,

15:15.003 --> 15:19.540
the idea of allowing
your own crucifixion.

15:24.378 --> 15:25.682
But you're not a Christian.

15:25.716 --> 15:28.250
So what do you believe?

15:28.283 --> 15:29.385
I believe that people
shouldn't talk

15:29.418 --> 15:31.352
about this type of shit at work.

15:31.385 --> 15:34.122
Hold on, hold on.

15:34.155 --> 15:36.891
Uh... 3 months
we been together,

15:36.924 --> 15:39.026
I get nothing from you.

15:39.059 --> 15:42.839
Today, what we're into now,

15:42.872 --> 15:44.039
do me a courtesy, okay?

15:44.072 --> 15:45.901
I'm not trying to convert you.

15:45.942 --> 15:48.172
Look. I consider myself
a realist, all right,

15:48.205 --> 15:51.709
but in philosophical terms,
I'm what's called a pessimist.

15:51.742 --> 15:54.580
Um, okay.
What's that mean?

15:54.613 --> 15:57.149
Means I'm bad at parties.

15:57.182 --> 15:59.519
Heh. Let me tell you.

15:59.552 --> 16:02.724
You ain't great outside
of parties either.

16:08.831 --> 16:11.199
I think human consciousness

16:11.232 --> 16:13.704
was a tragic misstep
in evolution.

16:13.737 --> 16:16.242
We became too self-aware.

16:16.275 --> 16:19.779
Nature created an aspect of
nature separate from itself.

16:19.812 --> 16:24.178
We are creatures that should
not exist by natural law.

16:24.219 --> 16:27.049
Huh. That sounds
god-fucking-awful, Rust.

16:27.083 --> 16:30.091
We are things that labor
under the illusion

16:30.124 --> 16:32.090
of having a self,

16:32.123 --> 16:36.489
this accretion of sensory
experience and feeling,

16:36.530 --> 16:41.834
programmed with total assurance
that we are each somebody

16:41.867 --> 16:43.971
when, in fact,
everybody's nobody.

16:44.004 --> 16:46.674
I wouldn't go around spouting
that shit, I was you.

16:46.707 --> 16:49.276
People around here
don't think that way.

16:49.309 --> 16:50.645
I don't think that way.

16:50.678 --> 16:52.979
I think the honorable
thing for species to do

16:53.012 --> 16:56.484
is deny our programming,

16:56.517 --> 16:58.686
stop reproducing,

16:58.719 --> 17:01.527
walk hand in hand
into extinction,

17:01.560 --> 17:03.824
one last midnight,
brothers and sisters

17:03.864 --> 17:06.998
opting out of a raw deal.

17:09.335 --> 17:12.801
So what's the point of getting
out bed in the morning?

17:12.841 --> 17:14.809
I tell myself I bear witness,

17:14.842 --> 17:19.437
but the real answer is that
it's obviously my programming,

17:19.478 --> 17:22.880
and I lack the constitution
for suicide.

17:22.913 --> 17:27.081
My luck, I picked today
to get to know you.

17:27.121 --> 17:29.957
3 months, I don't hear
a word from you, and...

17:29.990 --> 17:31.260
- You asked.
- Yeah.

17:31.293 --> 17:34.826
And now I'm begging you
to shut the fuck up.

17:42.231 --> 17:45.798
I get a bad taste
in my mouth out here.

17:45.839 --> 17:49.672
Aluminum, ash,

17:49.705 --> 17:52.710
like you can smell
the psychosphere.

17:52.742 --> 17:54.005
I got an idea.

17:54.046 --> 17:57.678
Let's make the car a place
of silent reflection

17:57.711 --> 18:01.351
from now on, okay?

18:04.794 --> 18:07.815
_

18:10.725 --> 18:13.323
What should I bring for dinner?

18:16.967 --> 18:21.837
A bottle of wine would
be nice, I guess.

18:21.870 --> 18:24.572
I don't drink.

18:24.605 --> 18:27.244
Well, no, of course not, Rust.

18:27.277 --> 18:28.811
Listen. When you're
at my house,

18:28.844 --> 18:30.746
I want you to chill
the fuck out.

18:30.779 --> 18:33.749
Don't even mention any of that
bullshit you just said to me.

18:33.782 --> 18:35.212
Of course not, Marty.

18:35.253 --> 18:38.017
I'm not some kind
of maniac, all right?

18:38.050 --> 18:40.385
I mean, for fuck's sake.

18:56.834 --> 18:58.570
What'd you hear?

18:58.603 --> 18:59.741
Ask Cohle.

18:59.774 --> 19:01.277
You mean The Tax Man?

19:01.310 --> 19:03.478
You know, he's IA.

19:03.511 --> 19:08.283
This is State CID Homicide...
Detective Geraci.

19:08.316 --> 19:10.386
Yes, ma'am.

19:10.419 --> 19:13.285
I'm calling to ask
about that night...

19:13.325 --> 19:15.660
I mean, you never heard
any shit like this before.

19:15.693 --> 19:17.859
She had...

19:17.892 --> 19:20.534
antlers. Um...

19:20.567 --> 19:21.768
Fuck.

19:21.801 --> 19:24.270
This is... this is
the real thing,

19:24.303 --> 19:27.808
some "Halloween" shit.

19:31.041 --> 19:35.311
Well, we're gonna have to
do a press conference.

19:35.344 --> 19:37.783
What about him?
What do you think?

19:43.221 --> 19:45.926
Smart...

19:45.991 --> 19:47.895
aloof.

19:47.928 --> 19:50.433
Doesn't care
about making friends,

19:50.466 --> 19:52.666
but he's already
running with it.

19:52.699 --> 19:58.441
He's got a real...
real mind for it. Yeah.

19:58.474 --> 20:00.644
So you'd keep him on then?

20:06.084 --> 20:08.417
Both of us, yeah.
I would.

20:08.450 --> 20:11.549
All right.
You're still lead.

20:11.582 --> 20:13.855
The incident room is yours,

20:13.888 --> 20:16.886
and, uh, you do
the briefing tomorrow.

20:16.919 --> 20:18.925
Yes, sir.
Thank you.

20:24.263 --> 20:25.765
Hello, sir.

20:30.967 --> 20:32.675
Fuck that prick.

20:38.084 --> 20:39.180
Yeah. No. I couldn't
hear you there.

20:39.213 --> 20:40.590
Antlers and shit.

20:40.591 --> 20:42.851
That's my point,
I wanted you to see her.

20:42.852 --> 20:44.252
Yeah, you don't mark
up a body like that...

20:44.390 --> 20:47.323
She had antlers?
What does that mean?

20:47.357 --> 20:50.861
It was a crown.

20:50.894 --> 20:54.195
We'll do the briefing
tomorrow, guys, early.

20:54.228 --> 20:56.960
My guy does the AP Wire
asked about Satanism.

20:57.001 --> 21:00.399
It got Speece here. You're
gonna have his nose up your ass.

21:00.432 --> 21:02.933
Major was saying something
about a press conference.

21:02.966 --> 21:05.564
Well, guess I can count
my blessings, fellas.

21:05.605 --> 21:07.035
Thanks for that.

21:20.211 --> 21:23.353
Hey. You mind
if I skate? Ahem.

21:23.386 --> 21:27.517
I got some names
from Vice, prost farms.

21:27.550 --> 21:30.919
Check around on our DB.

21:30.960 --> 21:33.287
You want me to go with you?

21:33.327 --> 21:37.031
Nah. Just something to do.

21:37.064 --> 21:40.837
Yeah. You go ahead. I'll
take care of the paperwork.

21:45.005 --> 21:46.476
Like I said,
I'm feeling a lot of stuff

21:46.509 --> 21:49.012
hit me at this time...

21:49.045 --> 21:52.718
my daughter's birthday,
this dead woman,

21:52.751 --> 21:56.187
and, um...

21:56.220 --> 21:59.052
figured I'd work
the case, you know,

21:59.093 --> 22:04.197
till DiCillo called
or we got an ID.

22:04.230 --> 22:07.829
State Vice gave me
some addresses to follow up on.

22:07.870 --> 22:11.470
So far, nobody'd...
nobody'd talked to me.

22:46.236 --> 22:48.673
Evening, ladies.

22:48.706 --> 22:53.033
I was hoping to ask
y'all a few questions.

22:53.066 --> 22:54.896
Oh, come on, man.

22:54.937 --> 22:56.199
I'll get the next round.

22:56.232 --> 22:58.997
Heh. You making
trouble for us then?

22:59.038 --> 23:01.268
No. I'm just looking to
get some information

23:01.301 --> 23:02.539
on a woman.

23:02.572 --> 23:03.803
Might be you know her.

23:03.836 --> 23:04.875
Who's that?

23:04.908 --> 23:08.243
Hold on.

23:08.276 --> 23:12.376
Mmm. We'll take two large
Long Island ice teas, please.

23:14.712 --> 23:16.077
Ma'am.

23:54.741 --> 23:56.940
I'm Rust, by the way.

23:56.973 --> 23:59.612
I'm Anette, she's Lucy.

24:01.288 --> 24:03.351
Either one of you know a woman

24:03.384 --> 24:06.923
about your age,
works the same place,

24:06.964 --> 24:11.231
about 5'5", blond like you?

24:11.272 --> 24:13.133
What kind of tits she have?

24:16.704 --> 24:19.648
Medium, a little larger
than yours,

24:19.681 --> 24:21.614
proportion to the body natural.

24:21.647 --> 24:22.780
Hmm.

24:22.813 --> 24:24.612
Gee. I don't know. We
see a lot of girls

24:24.645 --> 24:27.379
like that around.

24:27.412 --> 24:29.053
Any girls like that

24:29.086 --> 24:32.748
you haven't seen around
lately, missing like?

24:32.781 --> 24:35.949
People come and go.

24:35.982 --> 24:39.513
What do you want them for?

24:39.554 --> 24:43.154
I wouldn't bust
somebody for hooking

24:43.187 --> 24:44.825
or drugs.

24:47.992 --> 24:50.190
I'm murder police.

24:50.223 --> 24:53.295
Somebody got killed.

24:53.328 --> 24:54.663
There's a girl named Liza,

24:54.696 --> 24:55.927
another called Destiny,

24:55.968 --> 24:59.001
but I seen Destiny
yesterday at McDonald's.

24:59.034 --> 25:00.370
What about Liza?

25:00.403 --> 25:01.507
She's here.

25:12.350 --> 25:13.925
Anette, go get
a couple more drinks

25:13.958 --> 25:16.050
from the bar, will you, please?

25:19.021 --> 25:20.355
All right.

25:26.628 --> 25:28.658
You get pills pretty easy?

25:32.330 --> 25:35.128
Relax. I want some.

25:37.200 --> 25:38.230
Speed?

25:38.263 --> 25:41.763
No. Quaaludes,
anything-barbital.

25:41.796 --> 25:43.036
Uppers are easier to get,

25:43.069 --> 25:44.900
and they last longer, too.

25:44.933 --> 25:47.667
Yeah, but it's not like that.

25:47.707 --> 25:50.170
What's it like?

25:50.203 --> 25:52.810
I don't sleep.

26:25.975 --> 26:28.111
Hey.

26:28.144 --> 26:29.375
Oh.

26:29.408 --> 26:30.847
Hey, Lone Ranger.

26:30.880 --> 26:35.985
Hey. Ugh. Dreaming.

26:36.018 --> 26:38.585
Why you out here, huh?

26:38.618 --> 26:41.259
Why didn't you come to bed?

26:41.292 --> 26:42.723
Um...

26:46.932 --> 26:52.772
Caught a... bad one
yesterday.

26:52.805 --> 26:54.541
Just couldn't sleep.

26:54.574 --> 26:56.645
You got that woman from Erath?

26:56.678 --> 26:58.613
- Yeah.
- Yeah?

26:58.646 --> 27:00.076
Saw it on the news.

27:04.214 --> 27:05.822
Girls will be up soon.

27:08.286 --> 27:10.958
Missed you the last couple days.

27:10.991 --> 27:15.126
Oh, shit.
I got to shower.

27:15.167 --> 27:17.166
Got a debriefing today

27:17.199 --> 27:19.732
and maybe
a press conference later.

27:25.804 --> 27:26.969
And if Speece calls,

27:27.002 --> 27:28.874
tell him I'm debriefing
the squad all morning.

27:28.907 --> 27:30.139
Well, Marty said
he was doing that.

27:30.172 --> 27:31.578
He is.

27:31.611 --> 27:32.642
Hey, beautiful.

27:32.675 --> 27:35.181
Morning, baby.

27:35.214 --> 27:36.884
Marty, how you want
your coffee, doll?

27:36.917 --> 27:39.085
Strong and black just like you.

27:39.118 --> 27:42.358
Prints came back.
Dora Kelly Lange.

27:42.391 --> 27:46.160
Priors for shoplifting,
possession, and...

27:46.193 --> 27:47.897
solicitation.

27:47.930 --> 27:49.695
Address outside
of St. Martinville.

27:49.736 --> 27:52.069
Landlord says she hasn't lived
there in almost a year.

27:52.102 --> 27:53.364
She's got an ex Charlie Lange,

27:53.397 --> 27:55.667
who's doing 8 in Avoyelles
for bad checks,

27:55.699 --> 27:57.370
mom's outside of Breaux Bridge,

27:57.403 --> 27:59.537
DMV license expired,

27:59.570 --> 28:01.368
and DiCillo called.

28:04.809 --> 28:06.174
She was washed clean,

28:06.207 --> 28:07.971
not a print on her.

28:08.004 --> 28:11.409
We got ligature marks
on the wrists and ankles,

28:11.442 --> 28:12.872
was bound by a half-inch rope,

28:12.905 --> 28:14.975
maybe 10, 20 hours.

28:15.008 --> 28:17.775
Evidence of vaginal intercourse.

28:17.808 --> 28:19.447
Bound upright,

28:19.480 --> 28:22.047
hadn't eaten in a
day, maybe more.

28:22.080 --> 28:26.223
Toxicology hit for lysergic
acid and methamphetamine.

28:26.256 --> 28:29.120
That's crystal and LSD.

28:29.153 --> 28:31.129
How much LSD?

28:31.162 --> 28:32.561
Hard to say.

28:32.594 --> 28:35.465
Got to wait for a mass spec.

28:35.498 --> 28:39.433
So she was drugged, bound,

28:39.466 --> 28:42.170
tortured with a knife,

28:42.203 --> 28:46.747
strangled, posed out there.

28:46.780 --> 28:47.980
Yeah.

28:51.253 --> 28:53.115
What about this stuff?

28:53.148 --> 28:56.283
Well, the crown, for
lack of a better word,

28:56.323 --> 29:01.151
rose thorns, early
cane, switchgrass

29:01.192 --> 29:03.990
wrapped around a bent branch,

29:04.023 --> 29:07.492
and the horns are deer antlers.

29:07.525 --> 29:10.056
Again, no prints on anything.

29:10.089 --> 29:12.592
Symbols are painted
with acrylic basic blue

29:12.625 --> 29:14.296
using a thick glove finger.

29:14.329 --> 29:16.299
Ideas what any of this means?

29:16.332 --> 29:18.603
I don't know.

29:18.636 --> 29:22.104
And it's all primitive.
It's like cave paintings.

29:22.137 --> 29:24.570
Maybe you ought to talk
to an anthropologist.

29:39.019 --> 29:41.523
Lot of trouble this guy went to.

29:41.556 --> 29:44.025
Seems real personal.

29:44.058 --> 29:46.530
I don't think so.

29:46.563 --> 29:50.004
Was iconic, planned...

29:50.037 --> 29:52.540
and in some ways,
it was impersonal.

29:52.573 --> 29:55.173
Think of the blindfold.

29:59.046 --> 30:01.516
This place is
like somebody's memory

30:01.549 --> 30:04.452
of the town,
and the memory's fading.

30:04.485 --> 30:07.021
It's like there was never
anything here but jungle.

30:08.518 --> 30:12.189
Stop saying shit like that.
It's unprofessional.

30:12.222 --> 30:14.924
Oh, is that what
I'm going for here?

30:14.957 --> 30:17.929
I just want you to stop
saying odd shit,

30:17.963 --> 30:19.928
like you smell a psycho's fear

30:19.962 --> 30:22.434
or you're in someone's
faded memory of a town.

30:22.467 --> 30:23.467
Just stop.

30:23.469 --> 30:25.436
Well, given how long
it's taken for me

30:25.469 --> 30:27.435
to reconcile my nature,
I can't figure

30:27.468 --> 30:29.906
I'd forgo it
on your account, Marty.

30:41.954 --> 30:43.554
Ahem.

30:46.427 --> 30:48.921
You get any sleep last night?

30:48.954 --> 30:50.931
I don't sleep.

30:50.964 --> 30:53.068
I just dream.

30:54.967 --> 30:56.871
Occult.

30:56.904 --> 30:59.873
Now, I don't know if this shit
is anything but crazy,

30:59.914 --> 31:01.881
but Speece
and the Superintendent,

31:01.914 --> 31:05.282
they're paying attention,
the newspapers are making hay,

31:05.315 --> 31:07.283
church groups.

31:07.324 --> 31:09.289
Detective?

31:09.322 --> 31:11.258
Ahem.

31:11.291 --> 31:13.260
All right, here's
what we got so far.

31:13.293 --> 31:16.731
Deceased's name is
Dora Kelly Lange, 28...

31:16.764 --> 31:19.468
You stay busy now, the business?

31:19.501 --> 31:21.929
Well, yeah,
I got the security firm,

31:21.970 --> 31:24.466
PI stuff. Routine.

31:24.499 --> 31:26.941
Lotta guys leave the job,

31:26.974 --> 31:29.613
cemetery within 10.

31:29.646 --> 31:32.580
No family, idle hands.

31:32.613 --> 31:36.619
Some advice, you make it out,
you stay busy.

31:36.652 --> 31:38.586
Hit the corners.

31:38.619 --> 31:41.082
Ask about anybody
she was seeing...

31:41.123 --> 31:44.228
regular customers, meth dealers,

31:44.261 --> 31:46.722
and rough johns, anything.

31:46.763 --> 31:49.363
Any questions?

32:15.722 --> 32:18.321
You believe in ghosts?

32:21.194 --> 32:24.795
What'd we say about
silent reflection?

32:34.336 --> 32:36.809
You happen to hear
anything out of the ordinary

32:36.842 --> 32:40.081
between 10 and 1 AM, out back?

32:40.114 --> 32:43.017
No, no, but, uh,

32:43.050 --> 32:45.585
sometimes they, uh,
dove-hunt out there.

32:45.618 --> 32:48.088
They found a woman?

32:49.489 --> 32:51.223
Is it the Fontenot girl?

32:51.256 --> 32:52.654
Who?

32:52.687 --> 32:55.424
- And why would you ask that?
- Don't know.

32:55.457 --> 32:57.960
Went missing
around here years back.

32:57.993 --> 33:00.065
Last time something happened.

33:00.098 --> 33:02.064
Just thought maybe it's her.

33:02.097 --> 33:04.063
How old was she, this girl?

33:04.104 --> 33:06.240
I don't know.
Little.

33:07.610 --> 33:10.576
You know where the family lives?

33:20.152 --> 33:23.749
Had a place couple streets down.

33:25.023 --> 33:28.128
They moved out, though.

33:28.161 --> 33:30.694
Do you know the Fontenot
girl, one went missing?

33:30.726 --> 33:32.660
Her?

33:32.693 --> 33:35.163
Her family come to our service

33:35.196 --> 33:37.667
once or twice,
5 or 6 years back.

33:37.700 --> 33:40.531
Is that the girl?
Oh, Lord.

33:40.564 --> 33:43.101
No, sir, it's not.

33:43.142 --> 33:45.573
Excuse me.

33:45.606 --> 33:48.446
I want to ask y'all
something. Y'all think

33:48.479 --> 33:50.677
maybe this have something
to do with those cats?

33:50.710 --> 33:52.150
What cats?

33:52.183 --> 33:54.151
Two of 'em... one,
and a couple

33:54.184 --> 33:55.656
of weeks later, another.

33:55.689 --> 33:57.153
Somebody cut 'em up,

33:57.186 --> 33:59.161
turned their insides out,
then nailed them

33:59.194 --> 34:00.860
to the front door, twice.

34:00.893 --> 34:03.299
Now, I called
and told the police,

34:03.332 --> 34:06.331
but we're predominantly African
American congregation.

34:06.365 --> 34:09.102
I asked for it
to be investigated.

34:09.143 --> 34:12.712
We're not those type
of police, sir.

34:12.745 --> 34:15.616
Well, who is, then?

34:19.489 --> 34:22.117
Can I ask you something?

34:25.324 --> 34:27.789
Any of these look
familiar to you?

34:27.822 --> 34:29.787
- Seen them anywheres?
- No.

34:29.828 --> 34:31.792
No, they look like
something that might be

34:31.826 --> 34:33.792
carved into a tree or something.

34:33.825 --> 34:35.865
Mm-hmm.
How about these?

34:35.898 --> 34:38.864
Now, that look like
something my old auntie

34:38.897 --> 34:41.031
taught us how to make
when I was a tyke.

34:41.064 --> 34:43.198
What are they?

34:43.231 --> 34:45.703
Some folks call them bird traps.

34:45.736 --> 34:48.503
Old Auntie told us that
they were devil nets.

34:48.536 --> 34:51.839
You put them around the bed, catch
the devil before he get too close.

34:51.880 --> 34:53.806
That's interesting.

34:53.846 --> 34:56.244
- Hmm.
- She was a wonderful woman.

34:56.277 --> 34:59.314
Loved her some Jesus,
but had a bit

34:59.347 --> 35:02.311
of that Santeria
in her, you know?

35:02.344 --> 35:04.309
I always just thought
it was something

35:04.342 --> 35:06.551
for children to do,
keep 'em busy,

35:06.584 --> 35:11.020
tell them stories why
they're tying sticks together.

35:11.054 --> 35:13.792
Then that's all
we got on the Fontenot girl.

35:13.825 --> 35:15.792
There was nothing in there.

35:15.825 --> 35:18.328
Says, "Possible
report made in error."

35:18.361 --> 35:19.730
Now, that was 5 years ago.

35:19.763 --> 35:21.698
Ted Childress was
sheriff back then.

35:21.739 --> 35:24.199
He's set up in Gulf Shores
now, I think.

35:24.232 --> 35:26.669
Ten-year-old girl goes missing
and that doesn't go state-wide?

35:26.702 --> 35:28.670
Now, hold on now.
My understanding,

35:28.703 --> 35:30.673
the little girl went off
with her birth daddy.

35:30.706 --> 35:32.712
Now, did you check
her mom's record?

35:32.745 --> 35:35.144
Possession, solicitation.

35:35.177 --> 35:37.784
I believe Ted knew the family,
and the feeling was

35:37.817 --> 35:39.784
the little girl was
better off with her daddy.

35:39.817 --> 35:42.583
Mom seemed to agree;
she filed a complaint,

35:42.616 --> 35:44.589
then never bothered
with it again,

35:44.622 --> 35:46.421
took off with her boyfriend.

35:46.454 --> 35:48.923
R&I said you had
a complaint these parts

35:48.956 --> 35:50.924
around December...
little girl

35:50.957 --> 35:52.924
getting chased
through the woods.

35:52.957 --> 35:56.098
Oh, yeah, I pulled
that one for you, too.

36:03.339 --> 36:05.805
What the hell is this?

36:05.838 --> 36:08.308
Little girl said
a green-eared spaghetti monster

36:08.342 --> 36:10.813
chased her through some woods.

36:10.846 --> 36:13.685
Now, we had her work
with a sketch artist,

36:13.719 --> 36:15.783
and she told us
that looked exactly right.

36:15.816 --> 36:19.960
Now, you want to call an APB
on that, you go right ahead.

36:19.993 --> 36:21.960
Listen, boys.

36:21.993 --> 36:24.095
I'm gonna have to call
a timeout, make a beer run.

36:24.128 --> 36:27.296
Well, why don't you hold
off on that for a while?

36:29.171 --> 36:32.139
All right, well,
why don't you get it, then?

36:32.172 --> 36:34.641
We really don't want to do that.

36:34.674 --> 36:38.142
Well, is this supposed
to be admissible? Huh?

36:38.175 --> 36:42.141
If you want to pick
my brain, work a room,

36:42.182 --> 36:45.316
you buy me a cheeseburger
and a Coke, don't you?

36:46.685 --> 36:49.182
I'll take a sixer
of Old Milwaukee

36:49.222 --> 36:51.222
or Lone Star, nothing snooty.

36:51.255 --> 36:53.589
Why is this so important
to you all of a sudden?

36:53.622 --> 36:57.155
'Cause it's Thursday
and it's past noon.

36:57.188 --> 36:59.658
Thursday is one of my days off.

36:59.692 --> 37:03.166
On my off days, I start
drinking at noon.

37:03.199 --> 37:06.838
You don't get to interrupt that.

37:21.127 --> 37:22.727
Ahem.

37:24.096 --> 37:26.096
I'd appreciate a little
hustle up on that.

37:28.138 --> 37:30.073
Yesterday,

37:30.106 --> 37:32.242
at approximately 6 AM,

37:32.275 --> 37:35.747
civilians came across
the body of a female

37:35.780 --> 37:39.248
in a sugar cane field
outside of Erath.

37:39.281 --> 37:42.048
Now, this person,
we believe, was murdered,

37:42.081 --> 37:44.749
and we are not yet in
a position to

37:44.783 --> 37:47.751
release the identity
of the victim or to offer

37:47.784 --> 37:49.959
details of the crime.

37:49.992 --> 37:52.896
Our investigators

37:52.929 --> 37:55.393
have several leads,
and hopefully we'll...

37:55.434 --> 37:58.832
we'll have a suspect
for you in custody soon.

37:58.865 --> 38:01.336
Now, this perpetrator

38:01.369 --> 38:03.841
will be apprehended,
and he will know

38:03.874 --> 38:06.841
swift Louisiana justice.

38:06.874 --> 38:08.873
- Charlie?
- Mm-hmm?

38:08.914 --> 38:11.480
Let's talk about
your ex, Dora Lange.

38:11.513 --> 38:13.941
You want to talk Dori?

38:13.982 --> 38:16.350
What's she said I've done now?

38:16.383 --> 38:18.855
Nothing. We're just
curious if you knew

38:18.888 --> 38:21.391
what she's been up to and
maybe where she's living.

38:21.424 --> 38:22.991
Nope.

38:23.024 --> 38:24.992
Got her divorce papers
pushed through

38:25.025 --> 38:26.992
after I been here about a year.

38:27.025 --> 38:29.526
I don't blame the bitch.

38:29.559 --> 38:31.494
She got a habit?

38:31.527 --> 38:34.000
Yeah, a few.

38:34.033 --> 38:36.470
Weed, meth, juice.

38:36.503 --> 38:38.176
Name it.

38:38.209 --> 38:39.871
Charlie,

38:39.904 --> 38:41.342
how'd y'all meet?

38:41.375 --> 38:44.045
Growed up together,
dropped out the same time.

38:44.078 --> 38:46.680
Hitched up way too quick.

38:46.713 --> 38:50.014
You know how it is... you want
a wife, but only half the time.

38:50.047 --> 38:51.486
Hmm.

38:51.519 --> 38:53.993
Why are you saying
you hadn't heard from her?

38:54.026 --> 38:57.227
She called up here
for you not too long ago.

38:57.260 --> 38:59.300
She couldn't help me
anyway, man.

38:59.333 --> 39:01.237
She sounded all fucked up.

39:01.270 --> 39:03.238
You see, that's exactly
the kind of thing

39:03.271 --> 39:05.269
that we do want to know
about, though, Charlie.

39:05.302 --> 39:06.835
Oh. All right.

39:06.868 --> 39:09.909
Uh... I needed
some scratch for my store,

39:09.942 --> 39:13.042
and Dori owes me money,
she ain't got no fuckin' phone,

39:13.075 --> 39:15.683
so got a number to
her friend Carla, got her

39:15.716 --> 39:18.686
to call me back, and she ain't
made no fuckin' sense.

39:18.719 --> 39:22.486
Ahem. Carla's full
name and phone number.

39:22.527 --> 39:25.422
What you mean,
she didn't make sense?

39:25.463 --> 39:28.525
Like she could duck-hunt
with a rake.

39:28.566 --> 39:30.963
High, yeah.

39:30.996 --> 39:34.298
Talkin' 'bout
she's gonna become a nun.

39:34.331 --> 39:37.572
- Why a nun?
- I don't know, man. She was high.

39:37.605 --> 39:39.538
Fucked up, uh,

39:39.571 --> 39:42.907
talkin' 'bout...
she met a king.

39:42.940 --> 39:44.410
Shit.

39:44.443 --> 39:47.115
Anyway...

39:47.148 --> 39:49.285
I don't need no
snitch jacket up in here.

39:49.318 --> 39:51.823
Give me a break.

39:51.856 --> 39:54.322
This is Avoyelles.

39:54.362 --> 39:56.860
It's a goddamn day camp.

39:56.901 --> 39:59.598
Spend some time in Angola.

39:59.638 --> 40:02.529
Surprised you even got
Aryan Nation here.

40:04.104 --> 40:06.705
What'd Dori do?

40:10.013 --> 40:12.075
Dori's dead.

40:13.483 --> 40:15.946
Thank you, boys.

40:15.979 --> 40:18.616
We almost had a moment there.

40:29.561 --> 40:31.495
Mmm.

40:31.528 --> 40:34.896
So you want to talk the whole
case through or just the end?

40:34.929 --> 40:36.832
No, whole story

40:36.865 --> 40:38.231
from your end, you don't mind.

40:38.272 --> 40:40.503
You know, like he said,
files got ruined.

40:40.536 --> 40:42.136
Hurricane Rita.

40:44.504 --> 40:49.477
What he didn't say is that this
is about something else.

40:49.510 --> 40:53.981
Something new. That one
in Lake Charles, maybe?

40:54.014 --> 40:55.653
Now, why you say that?

40:55.686 --> 40:58.190
Get the details
out of the paper.

40:58.223 --> 41:00.161
Yeah, we did.

41:00.194 --> 41:03.023
You know anything about that,
about Lake Charles?

41:03.056 --> 41:05.592
Well, let me see

41:05.632 --> 41:08.299
what you got, jog my memory.

41:08.332 --> 41:10.267
Well, let's hear
your story first,

41:10.308 --> 41:13.441
see how it fit with what we got.

41:14.842 --> 41:17.609
Well, your dime, boss.

41:17.642 --> 41:20.041
Talking Cohle,
what about that dinner

41:20.081 --> 41:22.575
you mentioned, he turn up drunk?

41:22.616 --> 41:24.582
Oh. Yeah.

41:24.615 --> 41:27.044
Well, ahem.

41:27.085 --> 41:29.484
That dinner,
that was a bit later.

41:29.517 --> 41:32.085
It was kind of funny.

41:32.118 --> 41:34.589
The flowers, you know?

41:34.622 --> 41:37.555
Like, he read somewhere that
if you get invited to dinner,

41:37.588 --> 41:40.059
you're supposed
to bring flowers?

41:40.092 --> 41:42.093
The hell?

41:42.133 --> 41:44.630
You can barely stand up.

41:44.671 --> 41:46.595
What is it?

41:46.636 --> 41:49.037
You don't drink
with me or the boys,

41:49.070 --> 41:50.869
and you got to get a load on

41:50.910 --> 41:52.709
before you visit my family?

41:52.742 --> 41:55.276
No, Marty, it's not like that.

41:55.309 --> 41:57.811
And I didn't mean to,

41:57.844 --> 41:59.947
all right?

42:01.316 --> 42:03.786
And I don't drink
'cause I've had trouble

42:03.819 --> 42:06.953
with it before;
I didn't mean to.

42:09.355 --> 42:11.797
I was checking on a CI.

42:11.830 --> 42:14.965
I ended up hanging around a bar.

42:16.367 --> 42:18.301
I was sitting there.

42:18.334 --> 42:21.467
I couldn't think
of a good reason not to.

42:22.867 --> 42:25.600
Usually I can.

42:30.643 --> 42:33.010
Don't worry about it.

42:33.043 --> 42:35.011
Have some more coffee

42:35.052 --> 42:38.051
and just try to make 10
minutes of conversation.

42:38.084 --> 42:39.788
You got it.

42:39.821 --> 42:42.555
I'll call Chris or somebody,

42:42.588 --> 42:44.690
get you out of here.

42:46.563 --> 42:49.195
Marty.

42:51.499 --> 42:53.959
I'm sorry, man.

42:54.000 --> 42:56.433
Forget it.

42:56.466 --> 42:59.602
We'll try this some other time.

43:10.018 --> 43:13.983
Well, uh, Rust, it is
so nice to finally meet you.

43:14.016 --> 43:16.485
Sorry it took so long.

43:16.518 --> 43:19.484
Well, I tried to tell her
you aren't big on socializing.

43:19.517 --> 43:20.986
I said that your life's

43:21.019 --> 43:22.953
in this man's hands, right?

43:22.986 --> 43:25.425
Of course you should
meet the family.

43:25.458 --> 43:29.427
Well, not quite
as dramatic as that, hon.

43:29.460 --> 43:31.996
I've never fired my gun.

43:32.029 --> 43:34.037
Have you fired your gun?

43:34.070 --> 43:35.333
Audrey.

43:39.205 --> 43:40.643
Yes.

43:40.676 --> 43:42.507
You shot people?

43:42.540 --> 43:43.845
Macie.

43:43.878 --> 43:45.349
Ahem.

43:45.383 --> 43:47.851
Dad's never shot anybody.

43:47.884 --> 43:50.985
Well, that's good.

43:51.018 --> 43:52.882
You don't want to shoot people.

43:52.915 --> 43:54.650
But you have.

43:56.323 --> 43:58.794
Marty says you're from Texas.

43:58.827 --> 44:01.293
Yes, south Texas.

44:01.334 --> 44:04.767
I grew up in Alaska.

44:04.800 --> 44:07.533
Just been working here
the last 10, 12 years.

44:07.566 --> 44:09.541
What kind of work?

44:09.574 --> 44:12.342
Narcotics, mostly.

44:12.375 --> 44:14.310
Um...

44:14.343 --> 44:17.850
was on the Robbery Squad
in Houston until '89.

44:17.883 --> 44:21.690
Ahem. Oh. Be right back.

44:21.723 --> 44:23.826
Y'all keep eating.

44:28.196 --> 44:30.833
Do you like your job?

44:33.729 --> 44:35.904
Not exactly,

44:35.937 --> 44:38.105
but it's worthwhile.

44:38.138 --> 44:40.104
I'm good at it.

44:40.137 --> 44:42.239
You're not married?

44:43.640 --> 44:45.576
Once.

44:45.609 --> 44:48.082
- Uh, not anymore.
- Mm-hmm.

44:48.115 --> 44:51.521
Did you do this
while you were married?

44:51.554 --> 44:53.489
Hey, Chris.

44:53.522 --> 44:56.488
Hey, thanks for the page.

44:56.521 --> 44:59.524
Yeah, well, he'll appreciate it.

44:59.557 --> 45:02.018
Well... all right,

45:02.059 --> 45:04.754
then I appreciate it.

45:11.264 --> 45:13.199
Children?

45:13.232 --> 45:15.697
One.

45:15.738 --> 45:18.172
She passed.

45:18.205 --> 45:21.848
Marriage didn't last
long after that.

45:23.754 --> 45:25.851
Sorry.

45:27.725 --> 45:30.293
Ahem. Chris Demma's
on the phone for you.

45:30.326 --> 45:33.491
Something about a CI or...

45:33.532 --> 45:35.965
Back there to the left.

45:35.998 --> 45:37.966
- Excuse me.
- Of course.

45:42.203 --> 45:44.309
Ahem.

45:49.716 --> 45:51.643
What was that?

45:51.684 --> 45:53.685
What were y'all talking about?

45:53.718 --> 45:55.654
Your job.

45:55.687 --> 45:58.421
What do you know
about him, Marty?

46:01.327 --> 46:03.769
Um, not a lot.

46:03.802 --> 46:06.264
He could be a good detective.

46:06.305 --> 46:09.803
He's running on this
thing, but, uh...

46:09.844 --> 46:11.307
uppity.

46:12.845 --> 46:14.782
What?

46:14.815 --> 46:18.753
Jeez. Have you ever
asked him about himself?

46:20.157 --> 46:22.094
Baby, trust me.

46:22.135 --> 46:25.272
You do not want to pick
this man's brain.

46:29.180 --> 46:31.107
What was that?

46:31.148 --> 46:34.779
Oh, some details
on the CI. Ahem.

46:38.084 --> 46:40.725
Thank you for dinner, Maggie.

46:40.758 --> 46:43.558
- This looks great.
- My pleasure.

46:43.591 --> 46:45.556
I don't like that broccoli.

46:45.597 --> 46:47.091
Mind your manners.

46:47.132 --> 46:50.162
So you, uh, need to go or what?

46:51.530 --> 46:54.497
No, it's nothing can't
wait till tomorrow.

46:55.864 --> 47:00.135
Rust, uh, what
you were saying before?

47:03.009 --> 47:06.208
Oh, we can find something
nicer to talk about.

47:06.241 --> 47:09.682
Marty, I saw
your table in there.

47:09.715 --> 47:11.514
You fly-fish?

47:11.555 --> 47:13.653
Little bit.

47:15.092 --> 47:19.123
So you
and Cohle went bad in '02, huh?

47:19.164 --> 47:21.426
Heard about that.

47:21.459 --> 47:24.765
Yeah, well... what happened
between me and him

47:24.799 --> 47:28.773
don't have nothing to do
with Dora Lange.

47:30.142 --> 47:33.142
I worked with Rust Cohle
for 7 years.

47:33.175 --> 47:35.142
People change.

47:35.183 --> 47:38.414
Relationships change.

47:38.447 --> 47:40.920
You stay in touch?

47:40.953 --> 47:43.391
No.

47:43.424 --> 47:47.423
No, I haven't talked
to Rust in...

47:47.457 --> 47:49.931
10 years.

47:49.964 --> 47:52.132
Yeah.

47:54.605 --> 47:57.044
Look, however we...

47:57.077 --> 48:00.041
he was a good detective,

48:00.074 --> 48:04.043
and it don't matter how
he ended it. I mean...

48:04.084 --> 48:08.086
I can say that
because it's the truth,

48:08.119 --> 48:10.758
and I don't hold grudges.

48:10.792 --> 48:13.426
I believe that's the shit

48:13.467 --> 48:16.235
that leads to cancer.

48:20.109 --> 48:23.073
But why am I talking
about dinner?

48:23.106 --> 48:27.748
Y'all want to walk through
the Lange case, fine.

48:29.615 --> 48:33.424
This other stuff...
well, what's going on?

48:33.457 --> 48:36.326
Sorry. We just heard
some stories.

48:36.359 --> 48:38.358
Well, personally, I heard he was

48:38.391 --> 48:40.561
an ace case man, right?

48:40.602 --> 48:43.736
I'd like to understand
his process.

48:46.366 --> 48:48.333
"His process."

48:48.366 --> 48:49.974
Sure.

48:51.408 --> 48:53.488
The other landlord
says she trashed the place,

48:53.513 --> 48:55.479
so she lost her deposit.

48:55.512 --> 48:57.479
And the neighbors check out.

48:57.512 --> 48:59.985
Those that remember her
said that she, uh,

49:00.018 --> 49:02.490
used to come in early
in the morning,

49:02.523 --> 49:05.491
if she came home at all.

49:07.524 --> 49:10.668
You guys canvass the bars
pretty good today?

49:13.165 --> 49:15.637
You know, up your ass, Cohle.

49:15.670 --> 49:17.670
Why don't you do your
own fuckin' leg work,

49:17.710 --> 49:19.805
you rat fuck?

49:24.383 --> 49:26.046
Say it again, rummy.

49:26.079 --> 49:28.054
Hey.

49:31.552 --> 49:33.561
You know what, man?

49:33.593 --> 49:35.727
Fuck you,

49:35.760 --> 49:37.863
Tax Man.

49:41.403 --> 49:43.337
What the fuck?

49:43.370 --> 49:46.044
Ahem.
Back to point.

49:46.076 --> 49:48.044
Got 3 hits on working girls.

49:48.077 --> 49:50.548
No one close to her, naturally.

49:50.581 --> 49:53.914
A few names recognized
her as occasional.

49:53.948 --> 49:55.915
Like she tricked
now and then, show up

49:55.948 --> 49:58.725
at a couple of truck stops
when she needed cash.

49:58.758 --> 50:00.789
You got some names.
Which ones?

50:00.822 --> 50:04.293
I heard from my AP guy,
Ray Fontenot.

50:04.326 --> 50:06.830
Said her uncle's
Danny Fontenot...

50:06.863 --> 50:08.366
the pitcher, LSU.

50:08.399 --> 50:11.334
Yeah, I watched him
play. Great player.

50:11.367 --> 50:13.903
- Well, he lives close by.
- Ahem.

50:13.944 --> 50:16.039
Well, thanks, guys.

50:16.072 --> 50:18.542
What about you two?
Did you get anything today?

50:18.575 --> 50:21.579
- Not much, sir.
- Well...

50:21.612 --> 50:24.411
You might know
the Reverend Tuttle.

50:24.444 --> 50:26.579
He runs our state-wide
charity drive.

50:26.612 --> 50:28.588
This is Detective Hart,
Detective Cohle.

50:28.621 --> 50:30.083
Pleasure to meet you, Officers.

50:30.116 --> 50:31.586
Nice to meet you.
Cohle.

50:31.619 --> 50:34.586
Your case has a lot
of people taking care,

50:34.619 --> 50:37.626
doors locking where
they used to not.

50:37.659 --> 50:39.592
Eddie's been speaking
to me about it.

50:39.625 --> 50:41.294
Concerned, very concerned.

50:41.327 --> 50:44.066
We've been discussing
the viability of a task force

50:44.099 --> 50:46.571
to investigate crimes with
an anti-Christian connotation.

50:46.604 --> 50:49.405
You what?
Really?

50:51.807 --> 50:53.414
Yes.

50:56.186 --> 50:59.721
I don't mean to tell men
of your positions,

50:59.754 --> 51:03.425
but there is a war
happening behind things.

51:05.194 --> 51:07.358
Thank you for doing your part.

51:07.391 --> 51:09.598
- Thank you, sir.
- Yeah.

51:10.495 --> 51:12.932
Well...

51:12.965 --> 51:15.933
Eddie's going to be
very, very pleased

51:15.966 --> 51:19.102
to have such good men
working on this.

51:21.607 --> 51:24.079
Are you kidding me?

51:24.112 --> 51:26.583
Un-fuckin'-believable.

51:26.616 --> 51:29.049
"Anti-Christian."

51:29.082 --> 51:32.417
Fucks. And who
the fuck's Eddie?

51:32.458 --> 51:33.721
Huh?

51:35.124 --> 51:36.564
Is he serious?

51:36.597 --> 51:38.532
Well, he doesn't
have a television.

51:38.565 --> 51:40.499
- Who's Eddie?
- And he's from Texas.

51:40.532 --> 51:42.465
He's the fuckin' governor...

51:42.498 --> 51:44.466
- Edwin Tuttle.
- Ah.

51:44.499 --> 51:46.509
They're first cousins.

51:46.542 --> 51:47.974
Well, that makes sense.

51:48.007 --> 51:49.973
Yeah, that's the
sound of The Big Machine,

51:50.014 --> 51:52.340
Cohle, that's gearing up
to pound your ass.

51:52.381 --> 51:53.580
Heh!

51:53.613 --> 51:55.749
The sound of a gaggle of hens.

51:55.782 --> 51:57.749
Yeah, you better
watch your mouth

51:57.782 --> 52:00.054
or they're gonna
peck your eyes out.

52:01.590 --> 52:03.051
- Hi.
- Hi.

52:03.092 --> 52:05.219
I am looking for Detective Hart.

52:05.260 --> 52:07.429
I have a stack of
depositions for him.

52:07.462 --> 52:08.924
Judge Sutpen told me to
make sure and give them

52:08.965 --> 52:10.929
to Detective Hart
and no one else, so...

52:10.962 --> 52:12.729
- Oh.
- Is that the, um...

52:12.762 --> 52:14.195
The, uh, depositions.

52:14.236 --> 52:16.172
I thought I should
walk you through them.

52:16.205 --> 52:19.437
Oh. Great, great. Let's
just find a place to talk.

52:19.470 --> 52:20.943
Thanks, Cathleen.

52:20.976 --> 52:22.448
- Thank you.
- You're welcome.

52:22.481 --> 52:24.413
Right through here.

52:51.043 --> 52:54.043
Your victim was Dora Lange,

52:54.084 --> 52:56.580
but you all checked
on Marie Fontenot.

52:56.621 --> 52:58.051
Why?

52:58.084 --> 53:00.052
Missing girl, 5 years gone,

53:00.085 --> 53:01.558
report made in error?

53:01.591 --> 53:05.094
She had an uncle
who lived nearby...

53:05.127 --> 53:07.566
and call it intuition.

53:09.599 --> 53:12.565
Sometimes he's more responsive.

53:12.598 --> 53:14.803
I'd like to help.

53:20.709 --> 53:22.779
Mr. Fontenot all the way.

53:25.713 --> 53:28.148
Uh, ahem.

53:28.181 --> 53:31.223
We met,

53:31.256 --> 53:33.791
oh, maybe 7 years ago.

53:33.824 --> 53:36.297
I was visiting Skip Hays.

53:36.330 --> 53:38.801
I'd played for USL.

53:38.834 --> 53:42.167
Thing of beauty, sir,
watching you throw.

53:42.200 --> 53:43.670
Hmm.

53:43.703 --> 53:46.302
Danny, this man's a detective

53:46.335 --> 53:48.271
with the police.

53:53.047 --> 53:54.982
Uh...

53:55.015 --> 53:58.477
I'm actually...
Ahem. Sorry, uh,

53:58.518 --> 54:01.752
we wanted to ask you
about your niece, Marie.

54:01.785 --> 54:03.225
Hmm.

54:03.258 --> 54:06.657
"How much could You put on
one family?" I ask the Lord.

54:06.698 --> 54:09.527
We try to get by.

54:09.560 --> 54:12.062
Did you know Marie's
birth father?

54:12.095 --> 54:13.533
Len?

54:13.567 --> 54:15.661
Len Stroghes was her daddy.

54:15.702 --> 54:16.702
Hmm.

54:16.734 --> 54:18.366
It's okay.

54:18.399 --> 54:20.875
We're asking because, uh,

54:20.908 --> 54:23.378
we had heard that Marie
ran off with him

54:23.411 --> 54:26.745
and that... she wasn't
really missing.

54:29.284 --> 54:31.723
That's what Debbie said.

54:31.756 --> 54:35.725
Oh. Well, uh...
anybody heard from Len?

54:35.758 --> 54:39.366
Anybody maybe knows
where he's at?

54:43.237 --> 54:45.701
Uh, sorry.
The last thing.

54:45.734 --> 54:47.867
Do you know where Debbie is now?

54:47.908 --> 54:49.874
She married another man.

54:49.907 --> 54:53.378
Not the one she's
with when Marie...

54:53.411 --> 54:56.543
She was in Vegas, last we heard.

55:19.068 --> 55:21.570
Marie must have loved it here.

55:21.603 --> 55:22.904
Yeah.

55:22.937 --> 55:24.873
All this for her?

55:24.906 --> 55:26.874
Danny loved her so much.

55:26.907 --> 55:28.873
We weren't her legal guardians,

55:28.914 --> 55:31.407
but she played here
all the time,

55:31.448 --> 55:32.943
more than her Mama's.

55:32.976 --> 55:35.447
I can see why.

55:35.480 --> 55:39.492
What is it Dan has,
if you don't mind my asking?

55:39.525 --> 55:43.493
All they ever told us was
"a cerebral event."

55:43.526 --> 55:46.131
Series of strokes, like.

55:53.908 --> 55:56.005
Marty?

55:57.310 --> 55:59.950
Excuse me for one sec.

56:10.889 --> 56:14.022
Inside on the floor
on the right.

56:32.841 --> 56:34.873
I don't know what that is.

56:34.914 --> 56:37.978
I haven't looked in there
since the police first came.

56:45.525 --> 56:48.662
Bet you want
to hear the hero shot, huh?

56:49.967 --> 56:53.032
That place we carried
the kids out?

56:53.073 --> 56:55.168
Eventually, sure.

56:57.473 --> 57:00.608
So what did she look like...

57:00.641 --> 57:03.312
that one in Lake Charles?

57:27.583 --> 57:30.251
Can you, uh, tell us

57:30.284 --> 57:32.484
anything about that,
Mr. Cohle?

57:36.099 --> 57:39.065
That looks a lot
like the one from '95,

57:39.098 --> 57:42.205
but... well,
you knew that already.

57:42.238 --> 57:46.539
Yeah, there are specifics
consistent to the '95 case,

57:46.580 --> 57:50.044
details that weren't
public knowledge.

57:50.077 --> 57:53.053
You were off the grid
for 8 years, right?

57:53.086 --> 57:56.053
- Show back up here 2010.
- My question is...

57:56.086 --> 58:00.059
How could it be him...

58:00.093 --> 58:03.722
if we already caught him in '95?

58:06.131 --> 58:09.194
How indeed, Detectives?

58:09.235 --> 58:12.738
I figured you'd be
the one to know.

58:20.607 --> 58:24.574
Then start asking
the right fuckin' questions.
